On Thu, May 13, 2004 at 11:50:57PM -0400, John Cowan wrote:
> If you have "le le broda ku brode sa sa le brodi", what does that do
> currently?  Do you handle repeated sa's at all?

'sa' is only handled once; multiple sa are treated as though they were
one sa, so that sentence fails to parse.

I have no idea how easy it would be to make multiple sa go back to
multiple previous instances of the following selma'o.

